(1) The Minister may, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang make regulations which are necessary or expedient for giving effect to or carrying out the purposes and provisions of this Order and for the due administration thereof.

(2) prejudice to the generality of subsection ( 1), the Minister may make regulations for or with respect to all or any of the following matters - (a} the registration and regulation of foreign limited liability

(b) the powers and duties of the Registrar;

(c) the forms for the purposes of this Order, including the form of registers to be kept and the places at which the registers are to be kept;

(d) the translation of documents and records required for the purposes and the authentication and lodgment of any such translation;

(e) all matters connected with or arising from the restrictions as to the name which may be used by a limited liability partnership under this Order;

(f) the fees to be charged in respect of anything done under or by . virtue of this Order, and the method of payment of such fees;

(g) the persons or classes of persons who are to be exempted from the of any fee or part thereof;

(h) the penalties for the late lodgment of documents; (i} prescribing all matters and things which are required or which may be prescribed otherwise than by rules, under or for the purposes of this

(3) The Minister may, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang in making any regulations provide that any contravention of, or failure or neglect to comply with, any provision of the regulations or any directive by the Registrar pursuant to those regulations shall be an offence with a fine not exceeding $5,000, imprisonment for a term not one year or both and, in the case of a continuing offence, with a further fine not exceeding $200 for every day or part thereof during which the offence after conviction.

(4) In this section, "foreign limited liability partnership" means a formed, registered or incorporated outside Brunei Darussalam in the liability of the partners is limited, and having such other features as may be prescribed by the Minister. of Court.

His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan may by order make such provisions as may appear to him to be necessary or expedient -

(a) for giving effect into this Order;

(b) for the purpose of bringing any other written law into accord with this or with any order made hereunder. · Transitional and savings provisions.

(1) person who, being a past or present officer or partner of a limited partnership which is being wound-up - (aJ does not to the best of his knowledge and belief fully and truly ·disclose to the liquidator all the property of the limited liability partnership, and how and to whom and for what consideration and when the limited partnership disposed of any part thereof, except such part as has been disposed of in the ordinary way of the business of the limited liability (b} does not deliver up to the liquidator, or as he directs(i) all the property of the limited liability partnership in his custody or under his control and which he is required by law to deliver up; or

(ii) all books and papers in his custody or under his cqntrol belonging to the limited liability partnership and which he is. by law to deliver up; (c} within one year next before the commencement of the winding-up or at any time thereafter -

(i) has concealed any part of the property of the limited liability to the value of $200 or upwards, or has concealed any debt due to or from the limited liability partnership;

(ii) has fraudulently removed any part of the property of the liability partnership to the value of $200 or upwards;

(iii) has concealed, destroyed, mutilated or falsified, or has been privy to the concealment, destruction, mutilation or falsification of, any book or paper affecting or relating to the or affairs of the limited liability partnership;

(iv) has made or has been privy to the making of any false entry in any book or paper affecting or relating to the property or of the limited liability partnership;

(v) has fraudulently parted with, altered or made any omission in, or has been privy to fraudulent parting with, altering or any omission in, any document affecting or relating to the property or affairs of the limited liability partnership;

(vi) by any false representation or other fraud, has obtained any for or on behalf of the limited liability partnership on which the limited liability partnership has not paid for;

(vii) has obtained on credit, for or on behalf of the limited liability under the false pretence that the limited liability is carrying on its business, any property which the limited liability partnership has not subsequently paid for; or

(viii) has pawned, pledged or disposed of any property of the liability partnership which has been obtained on credit and has not been paid for, unless such pawning, pledging or disposing was in the ordinary way of the business of the limited liability partnership; {d} makes any material omission in any statement relating to the affairs of the limited liability partnership; {eJ knowing or believing that a false debt has been proved by any person, fails for a period of one month to inform the liquidator thereof; {fJ prevents the production of any book or paper affecting or relating to the property or affairs of the limited liability partnership; {g} within one year next before the commencement of the winding-up or at any time thereafter, has attempted to account for any part of the of the limited liability partnership by fictitious losses or expenses; or {h} within 12 months next before the commencement of the winding-up or at any time thereafter, has been guilty of any false representation or other for the purpose of obtaining the consent of the creditors of the limited partnership or any of them to an agreement with reference to the the limited liability partnership or to the winding-up, an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or for a term not exceeding 2 years.

(2) It shall be defence to a charge under sub-paragraphs (l){a}, {b), (l){c}(i),

(vii) or (viii) or {d) if the accused person proves that he had no intent to defraud, and to a charge under sub-paragraphs (l){c}(iii) or (iv) or ({} if he proves that he had no intent to conceal the state of affairs of the limited liability partnership or to defeat the law.

(3) any person pawns, pledges or disposes of any property in circumstances which amount to an offence under sub-paragraph (l)(cJ(viii), every who takes in pawn or pledge or otherwise receives the property knowing it to be pawned, pledged or disposed of in those circumstances is guilty of an and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years. Inducement to be appointed liquidator.
